-  <div class="section-label">// The Path Here</div>
-  <h2>From Service Implementation to AI Operations Leadership</h2>
-  <p>My career didn't start in AI — it started in the unglamorous work of making enterprise IT service delivery actually hold up under pressure. At Orange Business Services, that meant designing ITIL-aligned operational processes for telecom and financial services clients and being the final escalation authority when something went wrong. At Avaya, across nearly a decade, it scaled into running global service transitions and then owning end-to-end delivery for $10M–$25M managed services portfolios spanning APAC, EMEA, Africa, and North America.</p>
-  <p>What changed in the last three years isn't my focus — it's the toolset. The same discipline that drove 99.9%+ service availability and zero-Sev-1 transitions is now applied to building and deploying GenAI and AIOps tooling: Smart Desk, AI Incident Co-Pilot, and an enterprise RAG knowledge assistant, each grounded in real operational workflows rather than built as a demo. Leading AI transformation, to me, is still fundamentally an operations leadership problem — the AI is the tool, not the strategy.</p>
-</section>
-
-<section class="content alt-bg">
-  <div class="section-label">// Leadership Philosophy</div>
-  <h2>How I Think About Leading AI Operations Transformation</h2>
-  <div class="principles-grid">
-    <div class="principle-card">
-      <div class="num">01</div>
-      <h3>Governance Before Automation</h3>
-      <p>Automation built on top of weak governance just makes problems faster, not smaller. Every AI or AIOps initiative I lead starts with the access, data, and process foundation underneath it.</p>
-    </div>
-    <div class="principle-card">
-      <div class="num">02</div>
-      <h3>Consistency Over Heroics</h3>
-      <p>Portfolios and operations teams don't fail because people aren't talented — they fail from variance. I build standards that don't depend on which analyst, region, or week it is.</p>
-    </div>
-    <div class="principle-card">
-      <div class="num">03</div>
-      <h3>AI Augments Operators, Not Replaces Them</h3>
-      <p>Every production AI tool I've built — Smart Desk, AI Incident Co-Pilot — keeps a human in the loop for anything consequential. Trust is earned incrementally, not assumed.</p>
-    </div>
-    <div class="principle-card">
-      <div class="num">04</div>
-      <h3>Measure What Actually Matters</h3>
-      <p>MTTR, SLA adherence, auto-resolution rate — leadership decisions should be driven by operational metrics that are hard to fake, not by how polished the dashboard looks.</p>
-    </div>
-  </div>
-</section>
-
